From: tallbiscuits <112773728+tallbiscuits@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 07:55:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/14] Limits: only the velocity and acceleration the printer
 has

Halyard translates SET_VELOCITY_LIMIT into Marlin's maximum feedrate (M203) and
acceleration (M204), read from the printer. Marlin has no square corner velocity (its
junction deviation is a distance that depends on the acceleration), accel_to_decel or
minimum cruise ratio, so Halyard leaves them out of the toolhead and their fields are
hidden, with velocity and acceleration side by side. A Marlin that doesn't report its limits
has no max_velocity, and then the panel is hidden instead of showing made-up values.

